WEBVTT

00:15.432 --> 00:17.058
Say, Minato...

00:21.396 --> 00:23.815
What do you think of Koyun?

00:30.989 --> 00:32.365
I'd see her around.

00:33.241 --> 00:36.786
I figured she was different
from the other girls at school.

00:38.038 --> 00:39.330
So I remembered her face.

00:40.707 --> 00:41.833
Then...

00:46.755 --> 00:48.131
She's by herself again.

00:49.007 --> 00:52.010
I kept following her with my eyes
every time we crossed paths.

00:52.510 --> 00:54.012
I always thought...

00:55.263 --> 00:58.183
I guess I felt pity for her.

01:00.268 --> 01:01.269
Minato.

01:02.353 --> 01:05.315
You're always like this.
Aren't you, Minato?

01:05.398 --> 01:08.151
You're always pitying people.
"Poor you," or "She's alone."

01:08.651 --> 01:11.696
That is so sanctimonious of you.

01:12.280 --> 01:13.323
Sanctimonious?

01:14.532 --> 01:15.742
It is.

01:16.868 --> 01:19.537
Slapping a "poor you" sticker on someone...

01:20.121 --> 01:23.792
Do you have any idea how empty inside
that can make someone feel?

01:24.542 --> 01:27.962
You only do it so people look to you.

01:28.046 --> 01:29.881
You want them to depend on you.

01:30.882 --> 01:33.676
Do not try to wile your way in
with Koyun like that.

03:07.562 --> 03:11.983
EPISODE 4
IMPENETRABLE

03:12.984 --> 03:16.571
What gives you the right to decide
whether someone should be "pitied"?

03:17.572 --> 03:21.200
You shouldn't force Koyun
into some narrow mold you just made up.

03:22.827 --> 03:24.370
You may be right.

03:25.705 --> 03:27.206
But that was only at the start.

03:27.707 --> 03:29.125
Hikawa,

03:29.208 --> 03:32.378
I always thought,
"She is so pitiful." But...

03:33.421 --> 03:35.465
it was all just a misconception.

03:36.466 --> 03:37.467
Now...

03:39.302 --> 03:41.596
I'm in this for a different reason.

03:41.679 --> 03:42.722
So don't you worry.

03:44.015 --> 03:47.060
I don't think
you're quite her type, Minato.

03:47.143 --> 03:48.186
That's not what I meant.

03:48.269 --> 03:51.189
And even if it were,
you could at least sugarcoat it a bit.

03:51.689 --> 03:55.944
Well, whatever! Just don't go
getting close to Koyun for weird reasons.

03:56.027 --> 03:58.863
Surely we're allowed to
talk to each other?

03:59.447 --> 04:01.491
Why, are you her guardian?

04:02.533 --> 04:04.619
Spare the rod,
and you spoil the child, sweetie.

04:06.329 --> 04:10.625
I just don't want to hurt Koyun anymore.

04:11.334 --> 04:13.878
Not "I don't want her getting hurt"?

04:15.755 --> 04:18.132
But wait, the name "Hikawa"...

04:18.716 --> 04:19.968
Was she in the basketball club?

04:20.051 --> 04:20.885
EEK

04:21.469 --> 04:22.720
I knew it.

04:22.804 --> 04:25.056
Now I get why you were so angry.

04:25.139 --> 04:26.140
FLUSTERED, FLUSTERED

04:30.144 --> 04:35.066
This is exactly why I didn't want you and
Koyun getting involved with each other!

04:35.149 --> 04:38.152
Why can Yota get involved but not me, huh?

04:38.236 --> 04:40.780
Because you pick up on things!

04:40.863 --> 04:43.074
And what, Yota is oblivious?

04:43.157 --> 04:44.242
No, it's not that...

04:44.325 --> 04:45.576
That's a little uncalled for.

04:45.660 --> 04:46.661
I didn't mean that...

04:50.581 --> 04:51.666
Wow.

04:51.749 --> 04:53.293
They're so different.

04:53.376 --> 04:55.295
Yours is like a sumo wrestler's.

04:55.378 --> 04:57.297
What kind of comparison is that?

04:57.380 --> 04:58.423
Must be nice...

04:58.506 --> 04:59.674
Nice?

05:00.258 --> 05:04.137
I always wanted to palm the ball like this
when I was in the basketball club.

05:04.637 --> 05:06.681
But I just couldn't do it.

05:06.764 --> 05:08.808
Well, with those hands...

05:11.269 --> 05:13.396
Wait, huh? Basketball club?

05:13.479 --> 05:16.733
You were in the basketball club?
Why didn't you say so?

05:17.734 --> 05:20.361
I never played the way you do.

05:21.070 --> 05:22.989
I actually quit halfway.

05:33.583 --> 05:36.461
You mentioned feeling empty inside
at being pitied by others.

05:37.837 --> 05:42.759
Is that how you've felt
ever since I reached out to you?

05:42.842 --> 05:44.135
EEK

05:44.218 --> 05:45.219
FLUSTERED, FLUSTERED

05:45.303 --> 05:46.888
That...

05:48.639 --> 05:49.974
I'm sorry.

05:50.058 --> 05:51.893
You're right. I probably was pitying you.

05:54.103 --> 05:55.980
TOP GRADES GUARANTEED
CRAM SCHOOL

06:00.109 --> 06:03.571
I reached out to you because I thought
you looked bored there on your own.

06:04.572 --> 06:07.200
But now that we're friends,

06:07.283 --> 06:09.952
I don't see you in that way anymore.

06:10.578 --> 06:16.250
We became friends, Yota joined the group,
and we've had so much fun together

06:17.168 --> 06:20.171
that I was unable to see
that you were feeling this way.

06:21.506 --> 06:23.424
I'm sorry for hurting you.

06:26.469 --> 06:27.887
Minato...

06:31.057 --> 06:33.392
Why are you like this?
Personal distance, dude!

06:33.976 --> 06:36.479
I've enjoyed
our time together too, you know?

06:36.562 --> 06:38.606
And you've saved my butt heaps.

06:38.689 --> 06:40.149
Geez!

06:40.733 --> 06:43.152
So we gotta keep being friends, okay?

06:47.990 --> 06:49.200
Yep. Friends.

06:49.909 --> 06:51.285
You'll dirty your sweater...

06:51.369 --> 06:53.538
Don't worry. It's not clean to begin with.

06:53.621 --> 06:55.206
RUB RUB

06:55.289 --> 06:56.290
Excuse me?

06:58.292 --> 07:00.294
Now I get it.

07:01.212 --> 07:03.673
Maybe all I ever wanted

07:03.756 --> 07:07.927
was just to be friends with him
on equal footing.

07:11.264 --> 07:13.057
Man, I'm such a child!

07:15.226 --> 07:16.310
Miki?

07:17.186 --> 07:19.647
Geez! Wait up!

07:20.481 --> 07:22.942
They did go to get drinks, right?

07:23.025 --> 07:24.026
SLUMP

07:24.110 --> 07:25.611
They sure are taking their time.

07:25.695 --> 07:28.114
Do you think maybe they're out
growing their own cocoa beans?

07:28.197 --> 07:29.198
COCOA

07:29.282 --> 07:30.533
From scratch?

07:32.285 --> 07:34.704
Sorry to keep you waiting.

07:34.787 --> 07:36.247
DOUBLE EXTRA RED BEAN SOUP RICH

07:36.330 --> 07:39.667
Check it out. New products!
"Double Extra Red Bean Soup Rich!"

07:39.750 --> 07:40.835
We can share!

07:41.419 --> 07:42.837
Apparently, it's mandatory.

07:49.177 --> 07:51.846
Sounds like a ramen menu item!
This'll definitely clear my head.

07:51.929 --> 07:53.014
Right?

07:53.097 --> 07:55.933
This is just the pick-me-up we need
to get us through those exams.

07:56.017 --> 07:58.728
Did something happen with Miki?

08:02.565 --> 08:04.984
Should I even be asking her this?

08:07.069 --> 08:08.237
Miki...

08:09.322 --> 08:13.743
Did something happen between you
and Amamiya when you went to buy drinks?

08:15.661 --> 08:16.996
Well...

08:17.079 --> 08:18.623
A lot happened.

08:19.540 --> 08:22.668
We talked about that time
you bought that curry drink.

08:22.752 --> 08:23.878
Why?

08:24.462 --> 08:28.299
He said he made you buy it on accident,
so he was paying you back for it today.

08:28.382 --> 08:29.383
HE NEVER SAID ANYTHING

08:29.467 --> 08:31.135
What? He didn't have to worry about that.

08:31.219 --> 08:34.722
You see? He never said anything
because he knew you'd feel bad.

08:34.805 --> 08:35.848
- Bye-bye.
- See you.

08:35.932 --> 08:38.142
No! Feels like I'm losing
what we learned today!

08:38.226 --> 08:40.394
Wait... Notebook... I must review...

08:40.478 --> 08:43.064
No, wait! Don't leave my brain!

08:43.898 --> 08:48.069
Still, none of what she said just now
should have been enough to make her cry?

08:51.864 --> 08:53.991
The time for cramming for exams is over.

08:54.075 --> 08:55.159
SECOND SEMESTER FINAL EXAMS

08:55.243 --> 08:57.161
FIRST PERIOD: ENGLISH COMMUNICATION I
SECOND PERIOD: PUBLIC STUDIES

08:57.245 --> 08:58.788
It's the first day of exams.

09:01.415 --> 09:02.416
Begin.

09:08.589 --> 09:10.424
It really is exactly the same.

09:10.508 --> 09:11.676
Thank you, past exams.

09:13.678 --> 09:16.430
This is what we went through
during Yota's seminar!

09:16.514 --> 09:18.182
FIRST PERIOD:
ENGLISH COMMUNICATION I

09:18.266 --> 09:19.892
SECOND PERIOD: PUBLIC STUDIES

09:19.976 --> 09:21.936
THIRD PERIOD:
FUNDAMENTALS OF CHEMISTRY

09:24.272 --> 09:26.691
Off to a good start! Yay!

09:29.026 --> 09:30.945
SECOND SEMESTER
FINAL EXAMS - DAY TWO

09:31.028 --> 09:33.948
I've got it! I've got it this time!

09:43.249 --> 09:44.667
All right. Time's up.

10:05.021 --> 10:06.105
Messages.

10:06.188 --> 10:07.189
NINE
UNREAD: 9

10:07.273 --> 10:08.482
Wow, so many...

10:09.108 --> 10:12.570
Koyun! Let's grab lunch
before heading home.

10:12.653 --> 10:14.780
Oops, this is the group chat.
Wanna come, Yota?

10:14.864 --> 10:16.490
Oops, that wasn't an afterthought.

10:16.574 --> 10:18.034
Please join us. Whimper...

10:18.117 --> 10:19.118
LOL

10:19.201 --> 10:21.203
- I'll come.
- Koyun! Come on!

10:22.204 --> 10:24.206
Found you, Koyun!

10:26.709 --> 10:29.754
Looks like we're first to meet up.

10:30.338 --> 10:32.298
Do you think Miki
is still in the classroom?

10:37.011 --> 10:38.054
What's up, Miki?

10:38.137 --> 10:40.348
Hey, Minato. Where's Yota?

10:40.431 --> 10:41.599
He's already downstairs.

10:41.682 --> 10:44.018
Really?

10:44.101 --> 10:46.228
- Did you need him for something?
- Not exactly...

10:46.312 --> 10:49.398
Me and Koyun were just about
to go out for lunch with him.

10:51.233 --> 10:53.903
- What's this, Miki?
- You're freezing!

10:53.986 --> 10:56.947
Were you trying to leave me out of things?

10:57.031 --> 10:58.658
No! Not at all!

11:01.243 --> 11:03.162
Stare...

11:03.913 --> 11:06.999
Yeah, I'm totally stumped.
Are there really five more differences?

11:07.083 --> 11:09.168
- Number of grapes?
- Already checked.

11:09.251 --> 11:10.670
Found one.

11:10.753 --> 11:11.796
And here's another.

11:12.838 --> 11:14.924
Hey, wait! Minato, you're too quick.

11:15.007 --> 11:17.802
We gotta find them all,
or else our doria won't come.

11:17.885 --> 11:19.178
Is that how it works?

11:21.305 --> 11:24.475
They seem to be on good terms.

11:25.059 --> 11:26.435
That's good.

11:27.311 --> 11:28.938
Maybe I'm just overthinking things.

11:29.021 --> 11:31.941
SPACING OUT

11:32.024 --> 11:34.068
Have you been here before, Hikawa?

11:35.528 --> 11:37.530
Oh, no. This is my first time.

11:38.364 --> 11:40.783
I usually just go straight home
from school.

11:45.371 --> 11:47.706
Watch it with those pitiful eyes there!

11:47.790 --> 11:49.208
WELL?

11:49.792 --> 11:50.918
That's not it.

11:52.169 --> 11:54.338
- Thank you for the meal.
- Thank you for the meal.

11:54.922 --> 11:57.049
That was pretty tasty for being so cheap.

12:00.886 --> 12:03.889
You're not in any clubs, are you, Hikawa?

12:04.432 --> 12:05.683
Do you work part-time?

12:07.309 --> 12:10.229
Yeah. But I don't get many shifts.

12:10.312 --> 12:11.605
Where do you work?

12:11.689 --> 12:12.690
REGULAR CUSTOMERS

12:12.773 --> 12:13.983
Just a local restaurant.

12:14.066 --> 12:17.111
Only the local elderly come to visit.
It's very laid-back.

12:17.194 --> 12:19.363
What do you do on your days off?

12:19.447 --> 12:21.574
Come on, Minato...

12:22.908 --> 12:24.493
What do I do?

12:25.536 --> 12:26.996
I read...

12:30.249 --> 12:31.959
What's this? Looks lame.

12:32.918 --> 12:34.170
I watch movies...

12:34.670 --> 12:36.464
You like this stuff?

12:36.964 --> 12:38.841
I study ahead...

12:38.924 --> 12:40.092
You're such a nerd!

12:42.219 --> 12:43.679
I don't really do anything.

12:44.805 --> 12:47.183
I kind of just do a lot of nothing.

12:47.683 --> 12:50.853
Oh, really? That's a pity.

12:50.936 --> 12:51.937
GLARE

12:52.021 --> 12:55.149
Koyun gets super busy hanging out with me!

12:55.232 --> 12:56.484
Is that so?

13:01.780 --> 13:04.116
- Are you paying separately?
- Yes, please.

13:04.700 --> 13:06.827
Hey, Minato. What were you thinking?

13:06.911 --> 13:09.872
Why you gotta be so pushy?
I did tell you, didn't I?

13:09.955 --> 13:12.082
Yes, but...

13:12.166 --> 13:14.752
How boring must it be
if we're the only ones chatting?

13:14.835 --> 13:15.836
RUB RUB

13:17.087 --> 13:18.839
- You're right!
- You see?

13:22.843 --> 13:26.347
I get a little tired of all the questions.

13:28.933 --> 13:30.392
I am so full!

13:30.476 --> 13:34.313
I'm with different people, and the context
is completely different now,

13:34.939 --> 13:37.858
but I'm still not very good
at talking about myself.

13:39.360 --> 13:40.861
It's not that I hate doing it.

13:41.529 --> 13:44.490
I'm just scared of people
seeing the real me.

13:45.199 --> 13:47.326
I don't want to be rejected.

13:47.826 --> 13:50.955
I don't want to hate myself
more than I already do now.

13:52.331 --> 13:55.376
So when people reach out,
I keep my distance.

13:56.085 --> 13:57.920
You're weird.

14:00.130 --> 14:01.757
What even is "normal"?

14:05.469 --> 14:07.638
FINISH! SECOND SEMESTER
FINAL EXAMS DAY 3

14:07.721 --> 14:10.641
- Good job on the exams!
- Yay!

14:10.724 --> 14:12.643
EXAM AFTER-PARTY
IN GRADE 1 CLASS 5

14:12.726 --> 14:14.853
Want one? It's strawberry flavor.

14:14.937 --> 14:16.063
Thank you!

14:17.731 --> 14:20.943
Once again, Azumi is positively radiant.

14:23.487 --> 14:24.905
THUNK

14:24.989 --> 14:26.740
I feel awful...

14:27.241 --> 14:30.327
I managed to push through the exams,

14:30.411 --> 14:33.163
but my stomach is doing somersaults.

14:33.247 --> 14:35.165
NURSE'S OFFICE

14:35.749 --> 14:37.293
Noriko...

14:38.878 --> 14:41.297
You're just here to chill out again.

14:41.380 --> 14:43.883
This is not your private
little get-warm place.

14:43.966 --> 14:46.468
No... I'm actually sick today...

14:46.969 --> 14:48.304
Oh, my.

14:53.475 --> 14:54.643
My stomach hurts.

14:55.644 --> 14:57.104
Oh, dear. Is it stress?

14:57.187 --> 14:59.231
Or did you eat something off?

14:59.315 --> 15:01.775
I haven't eaten anything today.

15:02.401 --> 15:04.361
I did have three coffees though.

15:04.904 --> 15:06.447
That'll do it.

15:06.530 --> 15:08.699
Stay here and sleep until you feel better.

15:09.283 --> 15:11.785
I don't like the feeling of being in bed
in my school uniform.

15:11.869 --> 15:13.704
Well, beggars can't be choosers.

15:19.084 --> 15:21.253
Hey, got any of your old
middle school classmates here?

15:21.337 --> 15:23.839
Oh, yeah. A super nerd, that one.

15:23.923 --> 15:24.924
MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL

15:25.007 --> 15:27.176
Well, you gotta be smart
to get into Meiten.

15:28.427 --> 15:30.596
How about you, Igarashi?
Any old middle school classmates?

15:33.182 --> 15:34.558
Don't know.

15:34.642 --> 15:36.936
I doubt it. Who'd come here...

15:37.937 --> 15:40.689
We've got so many leftover snacks.

15:40.773 --> 15:42.066
Think we bought too many?

15:42.149 --> 15:43.442
Definitely.

15:43.525 --> 15:44.985
Hey, look. Students from West High.

15:48.197 --> 15:49.323
Igarashi?

15:52.868 --> 15:54.078
- What?
- What?

15:58.832 --> 16:00.125
What?

16:00.209 --> 16:01.418
Sorry, guys!

16:01.502 --> 16:04.338
You go on ahead.
I found an old friend from middle school.

16:04.421 --> 16:05.464
All right.

16:05.965 --> 16:06.966
Bye-bye!

16:07.716 --> 16:09.218
What are you doing here?

16:11.637 --> 16:14.431
Azumi. You...

16:16.684 --> 16:19.395
You've, like, completely changed.

16:19.478 --> 16:20.688
What happened to the gorilla?

16:22.022 --> 16:23.524
Shut up, you!

16:26.318 --> 16:27.403
Come here.

16:28.612 --> 16:30.656
Why are you here?

16:31.365 --> 16:33.283
For club. Club activities.

16:33.367 --> 16:35.703
Joint practice, you know?

16:37.371 --> 16:40.082
And hey,
I didn't know you got into Meiten.

16:40.582 --> 16:43.877
I'll bet you're the only one
who commutes this far every day.

16:44.378 --> 16:45.671
Why bother?

16:46.255 --> 16:49.299
Does he not know Koyun goes here too?

16:51.385 --> 16:54.304
Hey, Igarashi! What are you doing?

16:56.765 --> 16:58.684
- Sorry.
- See ya.

17:02.146 --> 17:04.565
Who was that? She's super cute.

17:04.648 --> 17:06.316
Are you blind or something?

17:06.400 --> 17:07.401
What?

17:08.110 --> 17:11.697
Koyun...
Please, please have gone home already...

17:17.036 --> 17:18.162
It's so dark!

17:19.038 --> 17:20.039
What time is it?

17:21.540 --> 17:23.292
Is it because the curtains are pulled?

17:23.792 --> 17:25.210
Thank you, Noriko.

17:25.794 --> 17:29.923
It's still light out,
so I can't have been out that long...

17:35.554 --> 17:36.805
Igarashi!

17:38.140 --> 17:39.475
That's right. It was today.

17:40.059 --> 17:43.645
Well, he's coming to our school, but
you wouldn't recognize each other then.

17:43.729 --> 17:44.772
When is that?

17:44.855 --> 17:47.649
During club activities on the afternoon
of the last day of exams.

17:48.567 --> 17:50.069
I knew this...

17:51.236 --> 17:52.404
Hey, by the way...

17:52.488 --> 17:54.990
I ran into Azumi earlier.

17:55.074 --> 17:57.409
Do you know her? Is she in your class?

17:57.493 --> 18:00.370
Miki? We're in different classes,
but we're good friends.

18:00.996 --> 18:04.583
Does she cause trouble here too?
No broken windows anywhere?

18:05.834 --> 18:07.169
She's fine.

18:07.795 --> 18:09.797
I ran into Azumi earlier.

18:10.547 --> 18:12.424
They're talking about Miki.

18:13.008 --> 18:14.009
Why?

18:15.302 --> 18:17.179
It's no good. I can't hear them.

18:19.014 --> 18:21.183
Hikawa? What are you doing?

18:24.311 --> 18:26.063
You feeling better now?

18:26.146 --> 18:27.356
I am.

18:27.439 --> 18:28.649
Ready to go home?

18:28.732 --> 18:29.942
Yes.

18:32.528 --> 18:34.905
I need to leave quickly
so he doesn't notice me.

18:38.283 --> 18:41.870
I couldn't quite catch it,
but they were talking about Miki.

18:41.954 --> 18:44.248
They wouldn't go on
to talk about me, would they?

18:47.626 --> 18:51.797
Amamiya wouldn't bring up my name...
Would he?

18:52.798 --> 18:54.508
Do you know a guy named Igarashi?

18:54.591 --> 18:55.801
Where do you work?

18:55.884 --> 18:57.594
What do you do on your days off?

18:57.678 --> 18:58.679
OBSESSED WITH OTHERS

18:58.762 --> 19:00.222
I think he will.

19:02.307 --> 19:03.475
I don't like this.

19:04.726 --> 19:07.146
I don't want people
to be interested in me.

19:12.818 --> 19:16.238
I don't want people knowing the real me.

19:18.907 --> 19:20.367
Hey. Igarashi?

19:20.450 --> 19:22.619
Do you remember Hikawa?

19:29.459 --> 19:30.836
Morning.

19:36.884 --> 19:38.010
Hey, Hikawa.

19:39.469 --> 19:40.554
Morning!

19:40.637 --> 19:41.638
WARM AND TOASTY

19:42.890 --> 19:45.142
He seems warm and toasty for some reason.

19:45.767 --> 19:48.145
Amamiya... Did you run here?

19:48.812 --> 19:50.856
We just finished morning practice.

19:50.939 --> 19:52.649
I must be steaming in the cold.

19:52.733 --> 19:54.568
Morning practice...

19:54.651 --> 19:56.403
I remember those days...

19:57.946 --> 20:00.032
By the way, Igarashi was here yesterday.

20:02.534 --> 20:05.787
But you're not interested in him, are you?

20:06.580 --> 20:08.707
I mean, you weren't all that close
with him, were you?

20:11.919 --> 20:13.378
Why is he being like this?

20:13.879 --> 20:17.382
Was Igarashi quite the prominent
figure in middle school?

20:18.258 --> 20:20.802
Yeah... I guess you could say that...

20:21.470 --> 20:24.097
He was always the center of attention.

20:24.181 --> 20:26.308
He was constantly surrounded by people.

20:26.892 --> 20:29.436
Yeah? I had a hunch he might have been.

20:30.020 --> 20:35.525
He's the kind of person who barges
into your heart without any consideration.

20:37.194 --> 20:38.195
I'm sorry.

20:38.779 --> 20:40.697
Maybe we should give middle school a rest.

20:44.284 --> 20:48.205
There's plenty of new memories
to make right here in high school.

20:48.288 --> 20:51.500
So many new events,
so we should look forward to those, right?

20:53.794 --> 20:57.714
I've never spoken to Amamiya
about my time in middle school.

20:58.548 --> 21:00.550
So why bring it up now?

21:02.886 --> 21:05.764
Did Igarashi say something to him?

21:06.807 --> 21:08.976
What did he say?

21:09.559 --> 21:13.105
Hey, are you and Igarashi going out?

21:13.188 --> 21:15.899
Yo, what base are you at?

21:16.692 --> 21:17.901
GIRLS BASKETBALL CLUB

21:17.985 --> 21:20.112
She is such a Pick Me, isn't she?

21:20.195 --> 21:21.321
I can't stand her.

21:22.489 --> 21:23.991
- Did you hear?
- About Igarashi...

21:24.074 --> 21:26.159
- At her house...
- No way, really?

21:26.243 --> 21:28.870
- So it's all true?
- No way!

21:29.454 --> 21:32.040
Why must people love to gossip so much?

21:32.749 --> 21:34.710
Why can't they just leave me alone?

21:34.793 --> 21:36.253
Hey, Koyuki.

21:37.671 --> 21:40.215
Is it really that fun to mess with people?

21:40.799 --> 21:42.926
Just tell us the truth already.

21:43.593 --> 21:45.387
You don't care about the truth.

21:45.470 --> 21:47.889
You only care that it's entertaining.

21:52.978 --> 21:54.229
No more...

21:56.732 --> 21:58.483
No more letting people in...

21:59.776 --> 22:00.777
Why?

22:02.112 --> 22:03.613
WARM AND TOASTY

22:03.697 --> 22:05.365
That cool air feels nice.

22:07.034 --> 22:08.035
Koyun--

22:08.118 --> 22:10.495
Why must you stick your nose
into other people's business?

22:14.958 --> 22:16.543
I don't get it...

22:19.838 --> 22:21.006
You disgust me.

23:50.345 --> 23:55.350
Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
